'''Takodana''' was a remote, neutral [[planet]] located in the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]], though it fell in the southwestern region of [[the galaxy]] known as the [[Western Reaches]].

==Description==
{{Quote|I didn't know there was this much green in the whole galaxy.|Rey|<ref name="TFA" />}}
[[File:Takodana_surface_1.png|thumb|left|250px|The landscape of Takodana]]
Covered in an abundance<ref name="SWTVE" /> of lush [[forest]]s<ref name="Visual" /> and dotted with small lakes,<ref name="SWTVE" /> Takodana, located along the [[Great Gran Run]],<ref name="TFA Locations" /> was a popular departure point that offered easy access to trade routes that connected the [[Inner Rim Territories|Inner]] and [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]]. For those heading outwards toward [[The galaxy|the galactic]] periphery, the [[planet]] was seen as a last taste of civilization, while those heading [[Core Worlds|Corewards]] saw it a last grasp of frontier living. Travelers found the planet's neutrality and distance from galactic [[politics]] appealing, and as a result Takodana became a haven for fugitives, [[smuggler]]s, and explorers.<ref name="Visual" /> Takodana was known as the longtime home of [[Takodana Castle]] that served as an open port to [[Spy|spies]] and dubious travelers alike.<ref name="Commander">''[[Star Wars: Commander]]''</ref> The world was connected to the [[Ring of Kafrene]] [[mining]] colony by the [[Biox Detour]] hyperspace route.<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" />

==History==
{{Quote|You know, here on Takodana&hellip; we welcome strangers&hellip; but you've already pushed our hospitality to its limits.|[[Savina Besatrix Malagán]] speaks to a Nihil marauder|<ref name="THRA 8">[[The High Republic Adventures (2021) 8|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2021) 8]]</ref>}}
[[File:Takodana_surface_2.png|thumb|right|250px|The ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'' arriving at Maz Kanata's castle.]]
Thousands of [[Standard year|years]] prior to the [[Cold War|conflict]] between the [[First Order]] and the [[Resistance]], a [[Battle of Takodana (Jedi versus Sith)|battle]] between the [[Jedi]] and [[Sith]] occurred on the planet. [[Maz Kanata]]'s castle would eventually be built over the ancient battleground.<ref name="Visual" /> The lower levels of the castle dated to the occupation of Takodana by the Jedi.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> Takodana fell under the control of [[Pirate Queen]] [[Maz Kanata]] via a plan that involved her conning the [[Geonosian]] [[Arkik Von]] out of Takodana, with the entire planet having been a score that Von was after. After her success, Von became obsessed with reclaiming Takodana&mdash;feeling the world was rightfully his&mdash;and continued to look for ways to conquer it for [[Standard decade|decades]].<ref name="Adventures 1">[[The High Republic Adventures (2022) 1|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2022) 1]]</ref>

During the [[High Republic Era]], Takodana hosted a [[Jedi Temple (Takodana)|Jedi Temple]] that was manned by the [[Kyuzo]] Jedi [[Savina Besatrix Malagán|Sav Malagán]]. The temple and surrounding area came under [[Battle of Takodana (Nihil conflict)|attack]] from members of the [[Nihil]] led by [[Krix Kamerat]], who wished to destroy the temple. Malagán proved more than a match for the Nihil forces, however, destroying most of their ships and prompting the rest to flee.<ref name="THRA 8" />

A year after the execution of [[Order 66]], [[Ahsoka Tano]] considered Takodana as a place to lie low after helping an attempted [[Raada Uprising|insurgency]], during which she revealed herself as a [[Force-sensitive]], on the [[moon]] [[Raada]]. However, she decided there were too many unknowns to staying on Takodana, electing to travel to the world of [[Thabeska]], where she had lived prior to arriving on Raada, instead.<ref name="Ahsoka">[[Ahsoka (novel)|''Ahsoka'']]</ref> Prior to being arrested on a ship in the [[Five Points system]], [[Jyn Erso]] spent almost a year on Takodana after bouncing around the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] on planets, such as [[Cerea]] and [[Coyerti]].<ref name="Rebel Rising">''[[Rebel Rising]]''</ref>

[[File:Acme-AttackonTakodana.png|thumb|left|300px|The Battle of Takodana underway]]
In the [[Standard decade|decades]] after the [[Galactic Civil War]], Takodana was the meeting place of [[Han Solo]], [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], and [[Finn]] with Kanata and her associates. While at the castle, Rey uncovered [[Skywalker lightsaber|Skywalker's lightsaber]], which called out to her in [[the Force]]. Not long afterward, their presence was reported to the First Order by [[Bazine Netal]] and a [[Battle of Takodana|battle]] ensued between the Order and the Resistance, who had earlier been alerted to the presence of [[BB-8]] by the undercover [[droid]] [[GA-97]]. Finn took up [[Luke Skywalker]]'s old [[lightsaber]] and fought for a short [[time]] in the area surrounding Maz Kanata's castle.<ref name="TFA" />

==Behind the scenes==
===''The Force Awakens''===
Takodana was created for the 2015 movie [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]. Director [[J.J. Abrams]] named the planet after [[Wikipedia:Takadanobaba|Takadanobaba]], a neighborhood in [[Wikipedia:Shinjuku|Shinjuku]], [[Wikipedia:Tokyo|Tokyo]]. Abrams stayed in a hotel in Takadanobaba the first time he visited Tokyo and named the planet as a nod to his favorite [[city]].<ref>{{WebCite|url=http://www.todayonline.com/entertainment/jj-abrams-reveals-star-wars-tidbits-tokyo|text=JJ Abrams' Star Wars secrets|author=Loh, Genevie Sarah|date=2015-12-11|work=Today|archivedate=20151214161949}}</ref>

Landscape shots of the planet were filmed in the [[Wikipedia:Lake District|Lake District]], in the northwest of [[Wikipedia:England|England]], [[Wikipedia:United Kingdom|UK]], in July 2014.<ref>{{WebCite|url=https://www.manchestereveningnews.co.uk/news/greater-manchester-news/star-wars-filmed-lake-district-10597811|text=Watch: Fascinating video pinpointing exactly where Star Wars scenes were filmed in the Lake District|date=2015-12-14|work=Manchester Evening News|archivedate=20180715210758}}</ref> "The landscape of Takodana" is a digitally modified view from over Watendlath Fell (54°31′12.74″N, 3°05′56.36″W) looking north across a digitally enlarged [[Wikipedia:Derwentwater|Derwent Water]], which is shown as contiguous with [[Wikipedia:Bassenthwaite Lake|Bassenthwaite Lake]] (which it was, briefly, in December 2015 after serious flooding). The large mountain on the skyline to the right is recognizably [[Wikipedia:Skiddaw|Skiddaw]], the fourth-highest summit in England.

"The ''Millennium Falcon'' arriving at Maz Kanata's castle" is a view southwest across the face of [[Wikipedia:Walla Crag|Walla Crag]] (54°35′14.06″N, 3°07′12.50″W), which overlooks the town of [[Wikipedia:Keswick, Cumbria|Keswick]]. Maz Kanata's castle is digitally added to the real Derwent Water, and the fells of [[Wikipedia:Cat Bells|Cat Bells]] and [[Wikipedia:Maiden Moor|Maiden Moor]] are clearly recognizable.

The forest scenes for Takodana, where Rey first encounters [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]], were filmed at [[Puzzlewood]], [[Wikipedia:Gloucestershire|Gloucestershire]], UK.<ref name="Star Wars Places">{{WebCite|url=http://starwarsplaces.com/locations/episode-vii/takodana|text=Star Wars Places – Takodana|work=Star Wars Places|archivedate=20180821234646}}</ref>

===Other media===
The planet Takodana also appeared in the [[2016]] non-[[Canon]] ''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Freemaker Adventures]]'' episodes "[[The Test]]" and "[[The Kyber Saber Crystal Chase]]." Both episodes made use of plot elements from ''The Force Awakens'' including Maz Kanata and her castle. "The Test" also introduced Takodana's [[Third moon of Takodana|third moon]], which was home to [[varactyl]]s.<ref name="The Test">{{FreemakerAdventures|The Test}}</ref> The existence of Takodana's third moon was at variance with the 2016 Canon reference book [[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']], which stated that the planet did not have a moon.<ref name="SWCL" />

